  "holistic_F_N": -1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are a mixed package: S1 imposes strict, immediate reporting and customer notice; S2 keeps a 5% new-model test cap but allows existing models above 5% to remain under open-ended regulator controls, with customer access to per-model results but no public publication; S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and a 6-year retrofit; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months with validated equivalents allowed; S5 sets an 8/100k review trigger but leaves recall to regulator discretion with no fixed transition, and only 'prompt' customer notices."
